# Git push
When the user says "push update" (or similar): stage and commit all relevant changes. The agent cannot run `git push` (no GitHub credentials in this environment). After committing, reply in one line that they should run `git push` locally—do not repeat long explanations.

# Links and navigation (CRITICAL — has caused 20+ hours of rework across athlete bios, Blue, admin profiles, States, etc.)
- **BLOCKER:** Links fail when (1) `<Link>` or `router.push()` is used inside Radix (DropdownMenu, Sheet, Dialog) — Radix intercepts the click; (2) same-site routes use `target="_blank"` — new tab often loads blank. Fix: use `<a href="...">` inside Radix; never `target="_blank"` for app routes.
- **Same rule everywhere:** Nav, dropdowns, athlete cards, admin tables, Blue page, NCHSAA/States, view-profile — if it’s an in-app route, follow this.
- **Inside Radix (dropdown, sheet, dialog):** Use plain `<a href="...">` only. Never `<Link>` and never `router.push()` alone. Radix intercepts and blocks navigation otherwise. Pattern: `<DropdownMenuItem asChild><a href={href}>...</a></DropdownMenuItem>`.
- **Never `target="_blank"` for same-site routes** (e.g. `/nchsaa/2026`, `/blue`, `/view-profile?id=...`). New-tab opens a blank or stuck page and has caused repeated “page never loads” issues. Use same-tab navigation unless the product explicitly requires “open in new tab” for that one link.
- **Before adding or changing any link:** (1) Use `<a href="...">` when inside a Radix menu/sheet. (2) Do not add `target="_blank"` for app routes. (3) Confirm the route exists. (4) Copy the pattern from a known working link in this codebase.
- **New pages:** Create the route first, then add the link using the same pattern as working items.

# Adding a new page (REQUIRED — nav links have failed 7+ times; follow exactly)
- **Step 1:** Create the route: `app/[your-path]/page.tsx` (e.g. `app/store/page.tsx` → `/store`).
- **Step 2:** In `components/navbar.tsx`, add the link using the **same pattern as Store/Cart**: force full-page navigation so nothing can intercept.
  - **Desktop (top-level):** `<a href="/your-path" className={navLinkClass("/your-path")} onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); window.location.href = "/your-path"; }}>Label</a>`
  - **Desktop (dropdown):** `<DropdownMenuItem asChild><a href="/your-path" className="cursor-pointer" onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); window.location.href = "/your-path"; }}>Label</a></DropdownMenuItem>`
  - **Mobile:** `<a href="/your-path" className={...} onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); setIsOpen(false); window.location.href = "/your-path"; }}>Label</a>`
- **Do not** use `<Link>` or `router.push()` for navbar/dropdown/sheet links. Do not rely on default `<a>` click — use `e.preventDefault()` and `window.location.href` so the link always works.

# Debugging (F12)
- Errors are logged with the **[RecruitNC]** prefix so they’re easy to find in the browser console. When something breaks, copy the F12 console output (especially lines starting with [RecruitNC]) and paste it; the agent will fix from the actual error instead of guessing.
